BelizeChain runs `pallet-contracts` (ink! 4.0) with `CallFilter = Everything` on a sovereign national chain. This means any deployed smart contract can dispatch any `RuntimeCall` that passes origin checks — including governance proposals, land registry operations, payroll entries, and compliance reports. On a generic DeFi chain this is an acceptable design. On a chain managing Belizean national infrastructure, it requires explicit security justification. This audit must determine whether `CallFilter = Everything` is an intentional policy decision or an unreviewed default.

