### RULE 4 — REENTRANCY TRACING IS MANDATORY FOR VALUE-HOLDING PALLETS

`CallStack = [Frame; 5]` allows 5 levels of nested contract calls. With `CallFilter = Everything`, a contract at call depth 4 can dispatch a RuntimeCall to a value-holding pallet. The classic reentrancy pattern:

1. Contract A calls pallet_belizex::swap
2. BelizeX calls back into Contract A before updating pool reserves (if it makes any external calls)
3. Contract A calls swap again with stale reserve data
4. Pool drained

This exact pattern requires BelizeX (or another value-holding pallet) to make an external call mid-operation. The auditor must verify whether any value-holding pallet dispatches to external accounts before completing its own state update. The answer may be "no" — but it must be verified, not assumed.

